This '''species''' was a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] that existed in [[the galaxy]].

==Biology and appearance==
This tall [[species]] was distinguished by their [[Rodent|rat-like]] appearances, with [[Color|brown]] skin, gray [[Hair|fur]], long fingers, elongated faces, and six [[eye]]s.<ref name="SC2" />

==Species in the galaxy==
Around [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{SkeletonCrewDate}}</ref> one [[Unidentified fry cook|member of this species]] worked as a [[Frycook|fry cook]] at a noodle shop on [[Borgo Prime]], attempting to capture the [[Youngling|children]] [[Wim]] and [[Neel]] after they tried to pay for a bowl of [[Unidentified noodle dish (Port Borgo)|noodles]] with an [[Galactic Republic|Old Republic]] [[Galactic Credit Standard|credit]], before they were beaten by the [[droid]] [[SM-33]].<ref name="SC2" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:FryCookCostume.png|thumb|right|250px|The fry cook's costume as seen on set for ''Star Wars: Skeleton Crew'']]
The species first appeared in the "[[Way, Way Out Past the Barrier]]," the second episode of the [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Skeleton Crew]]'',<ref name="SC2" /> which was released on [[December 2]], [[2024]].<ref name="Early">{{SW|url=news/skeleton-crew-premiere-date|text=''Star Wars: Skeleton Crew'' Will Debut Early|date=2024-11-26}}</ref> Concept art of the character was done by [[Aaron McBride]]<ref name="McBride">{{Instagram|username=amcb_toraidhe|name=[[Aaron McBride]]|url=p/DSE5f1fkYtk|date=2025-12-10|quote=Concept done for Star Wars Skeleton Crew ( 2024 ). Really loved working on this show! This was for the alien cook in the diner on Starport Borgo in Episode 2. Design Direction / Production Designer: Doug Chiang @doug_chiang|archivefile=File:Fry cook Aaron McBride IG.png}}</ref> and a costume for the species was made by the visual effects company [[Legacy Effects]].<ref name="Legacy">{{WebCite|url=https://www.legacyefx.com/skeleton-crew|text=Skeleton Crew|work=[[Legacy Effects]]' [https://www.legacyefx.com official website]|archivedate=20250226013146}}</ref>

